# Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) V1 Setup Guide

This guide details exactly how to configure your project to enable Push Notifications.

## 1. Get Firebase Service Account Key
To send notifications from the server, you need a private key.

1.  Go to the [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/).
2.  Select your project **"akr-ride"**.
3.  Click the ⚙️ icon (Project Settings) > **Service accounts**.
4.  Click **"Generate new private key"**.
5.  A JSON file will be downloaded containing your credentials.

## 2. Update Environment Variables (.env)
Open your `.env` file and add the following keys using the values from the JSON file you just downloaded.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The private key contains special characters like `\n`. When pasting into `.env`, ensure it is a single line string.

```env
# ... existing config ...

# FIREBASE ADMIN SDK (Required for sending notifications)
# From the downloaded JSON file: "client_email"
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx@akr-ride.iam.gserviceaccount.com

# From the downloaded JSON file: "private_key"
# fast way: Copy the content inside "private_key" quotes.
# ERROR WARNING: Ensure all \n are strictly literal string characters or handle them correctly. 
# Best practice for .env: pasting "Line 1\nLine 2\n..." is usually fine in Next.js
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nYour...\nPrivate...\nKey...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# OPTIONAL: Vapid Key for Web Push (Settings > Cloud Messaging > Web configuration)
# This is needed if you want to support web push properly across all browsers
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=Your_Vapid_Key_Here
```

## 3. Verify Setup
1.  **Restart Server**: Stop and restart your development server (`npm run dev`) so the new `.env` variables are loaded.
2.  **Test**: 
    -   Go to `http://localhost:3000`.
    -   Wait for the notification permission prompt (or check console for "FCM Token").
    -   Use the verification guide to send a test message.

## 4. Integration Details (How it works)
-   **Client**: `hooks/use-fcm-token.ts` gets the device token and saves it to Firestore (`users` or `restaurants`).
-   **Server**: Uses `lib/firebase-admin.ts` to initialize the Admin SDK using the variables above.
-   **Triggers**:
    -   **New Order**: Calls `/api/notifications/new-order` (Notifies Restaurant).
    -   **Order Update**: Calls `/api/notifications/order-status` (Notifies Customer).
    -   **Delivery Request**: Calls `/api/notifications/delivery-request` (Notifies Delivery Partners).
